{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Brings.ColourCubicDiscriminantValues","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Brings.ColourCubicDiscriminantValues","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Block","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Brings.ColourCubicDiscriminant"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.saddleTrinomial_discr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.saddleTrinomial_discr","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L245-L251","doc":"**The discriminant of the trinomial** `u³ − u + 2/5` is `−8/25 = −2³/5²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.saddleTrinomial_sylvester_lu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.saddleTrinomial_sylvester_lu","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L236-L243","doc":"`Syl = L · U` certificate for the trinomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.saddleTrinomialCoeffs_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.saddleTrinomialCoeffs_eval","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L230-L234","doc":"The coefficient vector is the corpus's `saddleTrinomial`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.saddleTrinomialCoeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.saddleTrinomialCoeffs","kind":"def","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L227-L228","doc":"Leading-first coefficients of `saddleTrinomial`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.reducedCubic_discr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.reducedCubic_discr","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L216-L223","doc":"**The discriminant of the reduced cubic** `16w³ + 24w² − 13w + 2` is\n`−80000 = −2⁷·5⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.reducedCubic_sylvester_lu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.reducedCubic_sylvester_lu","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L207-L214","doc":"`Syl = L · U` certificate for the reduced cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.reducedCubicCoeffs_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.reducedCubicCoeffs_eval","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L201-L205","doc":"The coefficient vector is the corpus's `reducedCubic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.reducedCubicCoeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.reducedCubicCoeffs","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L198-L199","doc":"Leading-first coefficients of `reducedCubic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSextic_discr_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSextic_discr_factored","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L192-L194","doc":"The same value as a prime factorisation: `−2¹⁹·5¹⁰`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSextic_discr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSextic_discr","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L175-L190","doc":"**The discriminant of the colour sextic**\n`16z⁶ + 24z⁵ + 35z⁴ + 50z³ + 35z² + 24z + 16` is `−5120000000000 = −2¹⁹·5¹⁰`\n(Sylvester-formula discriminant, see the module docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSextic_resultant_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSextic_resultant_int","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L163-L173","doc":"**The sextic's resultant with its derivative**, over `ℤ`:\n`Res(f, f') = 2²³·5¹⁰ = 81920000000000`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimV_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimV_det","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L158-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimE_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimE_det","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L154-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimV_upperTriangular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimV_upperTriangular","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L151-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimE_lowerTriangular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimE_lowerTriangular","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L147-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSextic_sylvester_elim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSextic_sylvester_elim","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L140-L145","doc":"The elimination certificate holds: `E · Syl = V`. Kernel-checked by `decide`\n(exact `ℤ` arithmetic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimV","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L136-L138","doc":"Elimination certificate, result: upper-triangular, integer entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSexticElimE","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L131-L134","doc":"Elimination certificate, left factor: lower-triangular, integer entries\n(a row-scaled inverse of the Doolittle factor of the sextic's Sylvester matrix). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSexticCoeffs_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSexticCoeffs_eval","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L125-L129","doc":"The coefficient vector is the corpus's `colourSextic`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSexticCoeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSexticCoeffs","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L122-L123","doc":"Leading-first coefficients of the colour sextic, over `ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colourSexticCoeffsZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colourSexticCoeffsZ","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L119-L120","doc":"Leading-first coefficients of the colour sextic, over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.eq_of_mul_eq_of_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.eq_of_mul_eq_of_eq","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L108-L115","doc":"Cancellation step used to read a determinant off an elimination certificate:\nfrom `e · x = v`, `e = cₑ ≠ 0`, `v = cᵥ` and `cₑ · r = cᵥ`, conclude `x = r`. Stated\nwith the determinants as opaque variables so that no tactic ever compares two\nconcrete determinants up to unfolding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.derivCoeffs_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.derivCoeffs_map","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L101-L106","doc":"`derivCoeffs` commutes with ring homomorphisms applied coefficientwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.sylvesterMatrix_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.sylvesterMatrix_map","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L93-L99","doc":"The Sylvester matrix commutes with ring homomorphisms applied coefficientwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.discr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.discr","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L88-L91","doc":"The discriminant of the degree-`N` polynomial (`N = d + 1`) with leading-first\ncoefficient vector `a`, by the Sylvester formula `(−1)^(N(N−1)/2) · a₀⁻¹ · Res(f, f')`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.derivCoeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.derivCoeffs","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L83-L86","doc":"Leading-first coefficient vector of the formal derivative of the degree-`(d+1)`\npolynomial with leading-first coefficients `a`: entry `k` is `(d + 1 − k) · a k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.resultant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.resultant","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L77-L81","doc":"The resultant of two leading-first coefficient vectors: the Sylvester\ndeterminant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.sylvesterMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.sylvesterMatrix","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/ColourCubicDiscriminantValues.lean#L64-L75","doc":"The Sylvester matrix of `p` (degree `m`; `p 0` leading, …, `p m` constant)\nand `q` (degree `n`, same convention). Rows `0 … n−1` are the coefficients of\n`p` shifted right by the row index; rows `n … n+m−1` are those of `q`, shifted\nby `row − n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}